    q: 'What is a Marketing Executive VA?',
    a: SITE.definition + ' One senior person owns the plan, does the work, and reports on it — instead of you juggling freelancers or paying agency overheads.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can one person really run my whole marketing function?',
    a: 'Yes — at small-business scale, marketing fails from lack of ownership, not lack of hands. One experienced operator running strategy, execution and reporting end to end beats a scatter of specialists nobody coordinates. When a job genuinely needs a specialist, I bring one in and manage them.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much does it cost compared to an agency or a hire?',
    a: 'A subscription costs a fraction of either. UK marketing managers average around £40,000+ a year before NI, pension and software; agency retainers commonly run £2,000–£10,000 a month. Tiers and what each includes are on the pricing page — no hidden extras.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will this work for my kind of business?',
    a: 'It’s built for owner-run businesses with roughly 1–25 staff — service businesses, local businesses, consultancies and DTC brands — where marketing matters but nobody owns it. The free intro call exists to answer exactly this question honestly; if it’s not a fit, I’ll say so.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much of my time will this take?',
    a: 'Almost none — that’s the point. After a kick-off call and a 90-day plan you approve, I run the work. You stay in the loop with a short monthly report and a call, not in the weeds approving every task.',
